## The 4 Core Architectural Pillars

All mobile applications delivered across the enterprise must implement the four foundational architectural pillars:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Architectural Pillar</th>
        <th>Standard Enforced</th>
        <th>Engineering Purpose</th>
        <th>Verification Method</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>1. Clean Architecture</strong></td>
        <td>Strict 4-layer model (Presentation, Domain, Data, Core). Domain layer has zero external dependencies.</td>
        <td>Decouples pure business rules from volatile UI frameworks and databases. Guarantees 100% portable domain testing.</td>
        <td>Danger PR code structure audit &amp; unit tests.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>2. Network Resilience</strong></td>
        <td>Threshold-based Circuit Breaker wrapping all remote HTTP calls with local offline cache fallback.</td>
        <td>Prevents cascading connection timeouts, stops battery drain, and maintains offline usability in dead zones.</td>
        <td>Automated unit tests with simulated 500/timeout responses.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>3. Remote Config &amp; Flags</strong></td>
        <td>Dynamic feature flags and emergency kill switches decoupled from store release cycles.</td>
        <td>Enables staged percentage rollouts (5% &rarr; 25% &rarr; 100%) and instant kill-switching without waiting for 72-hour store review.</td>
        <td>Integration with enterprise feature flag SDK.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>4. Hardware-Backed Security</strong></td>
        <td>OAuth2/OIDC SSO tokens stored in hardware KeyStore (Android) or Keychain (iOS). Zero plain-text credentials.</td>
        <td>Protects against binary reverse engineering, memory dumping, and stolen device credential exfiltration.</td>
        <td>NowSecure SAST/DAST automated security scanning.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

