## Architectural Non-Negotiables ("The Golden Rules")

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">MANDATORY ARCHITECTURAL ENFORCEMENT</div>
  <p>The following five constraints are programmatically enforced via CI and trigger automated PR rejection if violated:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1. No Direct Network or Database Access from UI:</strong> Views and ViewModels must never instantiate HTTP clients or execute direct SQL queries. All persistence and remote queries must be dispatched through Domain Use Cases.</li>
    <li><strong>2. Zero Framework Imports in the Domain Layer:</strong> The Domain layer must remain pure business logic. It must never import <code>android.*</code>, <code>UIKit</code>, <code>SwiftUI</code>, or <code>react-native</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>3. Mandatory Circuit Breaker on Remote Calls:</strong> All external API endpoints called from mobile clients must be encapsulated inside the enterprise Circuit Breaker.</li>
    <li><strong>4. Hardware-Backed Credential Storage:</strong> Auth tokens and cryptographic keys must be stored in Android KeyStore or iOS Keychain with biometric gating where required. Never store tokens in plain local storage or commit them in code.</li>
    <li><strong>5. Minimum 80% Unit Test Coverage on Domain Logic:</strong> All Use Cases, validation logic, and business rules must have automated unit test coverage with mock repositories.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

