## Architecture Decision Records (ADR) Process

When an engineering team proposes a substantial architectural change—such as introducing a new third-party dependency, modifying database engines, or altering authentication handshakes—they must submit an **Architecture Decision Record (ADR)** to the **Architecture Review Board (ARB)**.

### Standard Enterprise ADR Template (`docs/adr/ADR-0001-template.md`)

```markdown
# ADR-0001: Adoption of MMKV for High-Speed Key-Value Storage

## Status
Accepted (Date: 2026-10-14)

## Context
Our mobile application requires synchronous access to user preferences and encryption salts during app cold start. The existing async storage engine introduces 180ms of cold-start latency on Android devices.

## Decision
We will adopt Tencent MMKV as the enterprise standard key-value storage engine for fast, synchronous, encrypted access on both iOS and Android.

## Consequences
### Positive
* Cold-start storage read time reduced from 180ms to < 8ms.
* Built-in multi-process synchronization support.
* Transparent AES-128 encryption with keys managed in iOS Keychain and Android KeyStore.

### Trade-offs / Mitigations
* Introduces a native C++ library dependency (adds ~250KB to binary size).
* Mitigation: Pre-compiled binary verified by NowSecure and approved by Security.
```

